=begin
  exp_sagapanel.lic

  Saga-only panel tracking experience and Lumnis statistics in four sections:

    Overall Totals & Planning shows current progression, training points,
    Lumnis state, Tutelage, and RPA. Daily Grind shows Field Exp, gains,
    rates, pulses, and ETAs. Exp History shows persisted week/month/year
    experience, Ascension Exp, and ATP totals. History survives restarts and
    *exp importlogs can backfill it from prior session logs. Profession
    Resource shows the same type/weekly/total tracking as
    professionresource_sagapanel.lic (via Lich::Resources), off by default
    and toggled with *exp resource since not every character has one.

  Section headers and spacer rows only render when the preceding section has
  visible content. Both rows can be hidden with *exp ignore.

  Live values come from the native experience dialog. Field Exp deltas feed
  daily pace, pulse, hourly, and ETA calculations; decreases are ignored.
  Daily counters reset at 5 AM, and ETAs remain "--" until a gain is measured.

  Experience and Lumnis fields that are not pushed passively are refreshed
  every 20 minutes or with *exp refresh. Recognized command lines are parsed
  individually so unrelated game traffic remains untouched.

  RPA remains Active until manually cleared with *exp clearrpa.

  Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage shows Eligible, Active, or Ineligible from the
  current Lumnis stage and trigger messages. Lumnis Stage displays the
  active tier number in its row label.

  Red triangles hide individual rows, matching timers_sagapanel's *tm ignore.

  Field Exp's value is a <link> (clicking it runs *exp refresh) rather
  than a <label> like every other row, so Saga's panel font-override/
  color Settings actually apply to it, same reason
  commspanel_sagapanel.lic's rows are links. Wrapping its value in a real
  <output class="mono"/>...<output class=""/> pair (the same one the
  "experience" command's own report uses) was tried for fixed-width
  digit alignment but confirmed NOT to work -- Saga's dialog widget value
  attribute isn't parsed as XML the way the main text stream is, so it
  just showed the literal tag text. Reverted; plain text value, no mono
  formatting.

  Usage:
    ;exp_sagapanel.lic   - Start the panel

  Commands:
    *exp refresh              - Actively re-poll experience + lumnis info
                                 (queued -- runs on the script's next tick,
                                 within about a second)
    *exp importlogs             - Backfill Exp This Week/Month/Year from
                                 this character's own past session logs
                                 (see import_history_from_logs! -- day-level
                                 granularity, safe/idempotent to re-run,
                                 always skips today's still-open log)
    *exp ignore <field>       - Hide a row (also: click its red triangle)
    *exp unignore <field>     - Unhide a row
    *exp unignore all         - Unhide everything
    *exp ignored               - List hidden rows
    *exp tracked                - List currently shown rows
    *exp clearrpa              - Clear the RPA indicator
    *exp width <N>              - Set the value column width (gap before
                                 the red triangle) -- mirrors *tm width in
                                 timers_sagapanel.lic; entering the same N
                                 in both gives both panels the same
                                 gap-before-the-triangle look. Default 75.
    *exp resource                - Toggle the Profession Resource section
                                 on/off (off by default). Polls every 30
                                 seconds via Lich::Resources.check while on.
    *exp hidearrows              - Toggle the red row/spacer hide arrows

  Tags: saga, frontend, exp, lumnis, panel, efficiency, resource
  Author: Claude Code, RuseofFools
  Version: 1.13.2
=end

no_kill_all

require 'yaml'

module ExpPanel
  extend self
  include Lich::Common if defined?(Lich::Common)

  ROW_HEIGHT = 18
  LABEL_LEFT = 2
  LABEL_WIDTH = 134
  VALUE_LEFT = 142
  # Same +2 gap-before-the-triangle convention as timers_sagapanel.lic's
  # REMOVE_LEFT (DURATION_LEFT + DURATION_WIDTH + 2), and now user-facing
  # the same way too -- *exp width <N> (mirrors *tm width <N>) sets
  # value_width, which remove_left derives from live rather than a frozen
  # constant, so entering the same N in both scripts' width commands lines
  # up the same gap-before-the-triangle look in both, even though each
  # panel's own VALUE_LEFT/DURATION_LEFT differ. Defaults to 75 (was a
  # hardcoded constant before this was made adjustable).
  DEFAULT_VALUE_WIDTH = 77
  REMOVE_WIDTH = 20
  REMOVE_ICON = "&#x1F53B;".freeze

  # Gift of Lumnis tier -> stage number, per the user's own numbering.
  TIER_STAGE = { "doubled" => 2, "tripled" => 3, "quadrupled" => 4, "quintupled" => 5 }.freeze

  ROWS = [
    [:level,            "Level"],
    [:experience,       "Exp"],
    [:ascension_exp,    "Asc Exp"],
    [:total_exp,        "Total Exp"],
    [:long_term_exp,    "Long-Term Exp"],
    [:exp_next_tp,      "Exp to next TP"],
    [:eta_next_tp,      "ETA to next TP"],
    [:exp_next_atp,     "Exp to next ATP"],
    [:eta_next_atp,     "ETA to next ATP"],
    [:ptps_mtps,        "PTPs/MTPs"],
    [:atps,             "ATPs"],
    [:field_exp,        "Field Exp"],
    [:exp_today,        "Exp Earned Today"],
    [:avg_exp_hour,     "Avg Exp/Hour"],
    [:exp_last_hour,    "Exp Last Hour"],
    [:exp_per_pulse,    "Exp/Pulse"],
    [:best_pulse,       "Best Pulse"],
    [:hist_exp_week,    "Exp This Week"],
    [:hist_exp_month,   "Exp This Month"],
    [:hist_exp_year,    "Exp This Year"],
    [:hist_asc_week,    "Asc Exp This Week"],
    [:hist_asc_month,   "Asc Exp This Month"],
    [:hist_asc_year,    "Asc Exp This Year"],
    [:hist_atp_week,    "ATPs Earned This Week"],
    [:hist_atp_month,   "ATPs Earned This Month"],
    [:hist_atp_year,    "ATPs Earned This Year"],
    [:lumnis_donations, "Lumnis Donations"],
    [:lumnis_stage,     "Lumnis Stage"],
    [:lumnis_reset,     "Lumnis Reset"],
    [:fashlonae,        "Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage"],
    [:rpa, "RPA"],
    [:resource_type,    "Resource"],
    [:resource_weekly,  "Resource Weekly"],
    [:resource_total,   "Resource Total"]
  ].freeze
  ROW_KEYS = ROWS.map(&:first).freeze
  ROW_LABELS = ROWS.to_h.freeze

  # Same 3 fields professionresource_sagapanel.lic tracks (type/weekly/
  # total, via Lich::Resources -- Infomon's own profession-resource
  # tracking, e.g. Empath Vitality, Bard Luck Inspiration, etc.), gated
  # behind *exp resource since not every character has one (Warriors,
  # say) and polling "resource" for a character that doesn't is pointless
  # command spam -- off by default, unlike everything else in this panel.
  RESOURCE_KEYS = [:resource_type, :resource_weekly, :resource_total].freeze
  RESOURCE_WEEKLY_CAP = 50_000
  RESOURCE_TOTAL_CAP = 200_000
  RESOURCE_POLL_SECONDS = 30

  # Three panel sections: overall totals/state useful for planning (where
  # am I, how long until my next TP/ATP, what's my Lumnis/Tutelage status),
  # today's pace (how's THIS session/day going -- Field Exp lives here, not
  # in Planning, since it's a raw moment-to-moment meter rather than a
  # stable long-term total), and longer-horizon history (week/month/year,
  # persisted to disk -- see exp_history_path). A section with every one of
  # its rows hidden via *exp ignore doesn't render its header either --
  # same "only show what has content" rule timers_sagapanel.lic uses for
  # its category headers.
  SECTIONS = [
    ["Overall Totals & Planning", [
      :level, :experience, :ascension_exp, :total_exp, :long_term_exp,
      :exp_next_tp, :eta_next_tp, :exp_next_atp, :eta_next_atp, :ptps_mtps, :atps,
      :lumnis_donations, :lumnis_stage, :lumnis_reset, :fashlonae, :rpa
    ]],
    ["Daily Grind", [
      :field_exp, :exp_today, :avg_exp_hour, :exp_last_hour, :exp_per_pulse, :best_pulse
    ]],
    ["Exp History", [
      :hist_exp_week, :hist_exp_month, :hist_exp_year,
      :hist_asc_week, :hist_asc_month, :hist_asc_year,
      :hist_atp_week, :hist_atp_month, :hist_atp_year
    ]],
    ["Profession Resource", RESOURCE_KEYS]
  ].freeze

  # One blank spacer row after each section except the last, each with its
  # own red-triangle hide control (*exp ignore spacer_after_N) -- same
  # ignored-list mechanism as every real row, just not a ROWS entry since
  # it carries no data. build_dialog only actually renders a given
  # spacer_after_N if section N itself rendered something -- if section N
  # is entirely hidden, its trailing spacer has nothing to trail and is
  # skipped too, regardless of whether it's individually ignored.
  SPACER_KEYS = (0...(SECTIONS.length - 1)).map { |i| "spacer_after_#{i}" }.freeze

  # ATPs are earned at a fixed 1-per-50,000-Ascension-Exp rate (per the
  # user), so "ATPs Earned This Week/Month/Year" is purely derived from
  # the same Ascension Exp history bucket the Ascension Exp rows already
  # read, not tracked separately.
  ASCENSION_EXP_PER_ATP = 50_000

  # Rolling exp/hour rate is computed off "today" (resets at the same 5 AM
  # boundary uberbar_eo.lic uses for its own daily silver/bounty counters),
  # not off total session time -- so the rate reacts to a play-style change
  # (e.g. switching from hunting to crafting) within the hour instead of
  # staying diluted by however long the panel has been open.
  DAY_BOUNDARY_HOUR = 5
  # How far back exp_history/asc_history samples are kept -- a little past
  # 60 minutes so "last hour" always has a clean full window to sum.
  HISTORY_KEEP_SECONDS = 3660
  LAST_HOUR_SECONDS = 3600

  @data = {}
  @exp_history = [] # [[Time, gain], ...] -- fine-grained samples for "Exp Last Hour"
  @asc_history = [] # same, for ascension exp (drives the ATP-ETA rate)
  # {"daily" => {"2026-08-23" => {"field"=>N, "asc"=>M}, ...}, "weekly" =>
  # {...}, "monthly" => {...}, "yearly" => {...}} -- persisted long-term,
  # unlike @data's today/session counters which live only in memory.
  @history = { "daily" => {}, "weekly" => {}, "monthly" => {}, "yearly" => {} }
  @history_dirty = false

  @value_width = DEFAULT_VALUE_WIDTH
  @resource_enabled = false
  @hide_arrows = false

  class << self
    attr_accessor :ignored, :data, :history, :history_dirty, :value_width, :resource_enabled, :hide_arrows
  end

  # Derived live from value_width rather than a frozen constant, since
  # *exp width can change value_width at runtime -- mirrors
  # timers_sagapanel.lic's REMOVE_LEFT = DURATION_LEFT + DURATION_WIDTH + 2
  # exactly, just as a method instead of a constant.
  def self.remove_left
    VALUE_LEFT + value_width + 2
  end

  def self.settings_path
    base_dir = "#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}/#{Char.name}"
    Dir.mkdir("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}") unless File.exist?("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}")
    Dir.mkdir(base_dir) unless File.exist?(base_dir)
    File.join(base_dir, "lichwindows.yaml")
  end

  def self.load_settings
    filename = settings_path
    settings_hash = File.exist?(filename) ? YAML.load_file(filename) : {}
    settings_hash = {} unless settings_hash.is_a?(Hash)
    settings_hash["exp"] = {} unless settings_hash["exp"].is_a?(Hash)
    allowed_keys = ROW_KEYS.map(&:to_s) + SPACER_KEYS
    settings_hash["exp"]["ignored"] = Array(settings_hash["exp"]["ignored"]).map(&:to_s).uniq & allowed_keys
    width = settings_hash["exp"]["value_width"].to_i
    settings_hash["exp"]["value_width"] = width.positive? ? width : DEFAULT_VALUE_WIDTH
    settings_hash["exp"]["resource_enabled"] = !!settings_hash["exp"]["resource_enabled"]
    settings_hash["exp"]["hide_arrows"] = !!settings_hash["exp"]["hide_arrows"]
    settings_hash
  end

  def self.save_settings(settings)
    File.write(settings_path, settings.to_yaml)
  end

  def self.set_value_width!(width)
    return false unless width.positive?

    settings = load_settings
    self.value_width = width
    settings["exp"]["value_width"] = width
    save_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.set_resource_enabled!(enabled)
    settings = load_settings
    self.resource_enabled = enabled
    settings["exp"]["resource_enabled"] = enabled
    save_settings(settings)
    enabled
  end

  def self.toggle_hide_arrows!
    settings = load_settings
    self.hide_arrows = !hide_arrows
    settings["exp"]["hide_arrows"] = hide_arrows
    save_settings(settings)
    hide_arrows
  end

  # Separate file from lichwindows.yaml (settings) since this is
  # substantive historical data meant to accumulate indefinitely across
  # restarts, not a small per-window preferences blob.
  def self.history_path
    base_dir = "#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}/#{Char.name}"
    Dir.mkdir("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}") unless File.exist?("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}")
    Dir.mkdir(base_dir) unless File.exist?(base_dir)
    File.join(base_dir, "exp_sagapanel_history.yaml")
  end

  def self.load_history!
    filename = history_path
    loaded = File.exist?(filename) ? YAML.load_file(filename) : {}
    loaded = {} unless loaded.is_a?(Hash)
    self.history = %w[daily weekly monthly yearly processed_log_files].each_with_object({}) do |bucket, acc|
      acc[bucket] = loaded[bucket].is_a?(Hash) ? loaded[bucket] : {}
    end
    self.history_dirty = false
  end

  def self.save_history!
    return unless history_dirty

    File.write(history_path, history.to_yaml)
    self.history_dirty = false
  end

  # Restores today's in-memory counters from whatever was already
  # persisted for today's bucket -- without this, restarting the script
  # mid-day (e.g. to pick up a fix) would silently reset Exp Earned Today/
  # Avg Exp/Hour/Exp Last Hour back to 0 even though the day isn't over,
  # which looked identical to "pulse tracking isn't working."
  def self.restore_today_from_history!
    entry = history["daily"][day_key(Time.now)]
    return unless entry

    @data[:today_exp_gained] = entry["field"].to_i
    @data[:today_asc_gained] = entry["asc"].to_i
  end

  # Three independent components per bucket entry, tracked in parallel
  # rather than one combined total:
  #   "field" -- Field Exp gained (bounded meter, drives Daily Grind's
  #              Today/Avg/Last Hour/Pulse/Best Pulse -- see
  #              record_exp_sample). Not shown anywhere in Exp History.
  #   "exp"   -- lifetime Experience gained (the "Experience:" counter --
  #              see record_lifetime_exp_sample!). Drives Experience This
  #              Week/Month/Year.
  #   "asc"   -- lifetime Ascension Exp gained. Drives both Ascension Exp
  #              This Week/Month/Year AND ATPs Earned This Week/Month/Year
  #              (ASCENSION_EXP_PER_ATP) -- the same number, no separate
  #              ATP tracking needed since the conversion rate is fixed.
  def self.record_history_gain!(at:, field: 0, exp: 0, asc: 0)
    return if field <= 0 && exp <= 0 && asc <= 0

    {
      "daily"   => day_key(at),
      "weekly"  => week_key(at),
      "monthly" => month_key(at),
      "yearly"  => year_key(at)
    }.each do |bucket, key|
      entry = (history[bucket][key] ||= { "field" => 0, "exp" => 0, "asc" => 0 })
      entry["field"] = entry["field"].to_i + field
      entry["exp"] = entry["exp"].to_i + exp
      entry["asc"] = entry["asc"].to_i + asc
    end
    self.history_dirty = true
  end

  def self.history_bucket_component(bucket, key, component)
    entry = history[bucket][key]
    return nil unless entry

    entry[component].to_i
  end

  def self.period_bucket_key(period)
    case period
    when :week then ["weekly", week_key(Time.now)]
    when :month then ["monthly", month_key(Time.now)]
    when :year then ["yearly", year_key(Time.now)]
    end
  end

  def self.history_period_value(period, component)
    bucket, key = period_bucket_key(period)
    history_bucket_component(bucket, key, component)
  end

  # Maps a :hist_exp_week/:hist_asc_month/:hist_atp_year-style row key to
  # the :week/:month/:year period_bucket_key expects, off the row key's
  # own trailing word rather than a separate lookup table.
  def self.hist_period(row_key)
    row_key.to_s.split("_").last.to_sym
  end

  # Backfills week/month/year (and past days) from this character's own
  # plain-text session logs (LOG_DIR/<Game>-<CharName>/**/*.log) by
  # scanning the same three lines the user pasted from a real "experience"
  # report -- "Experience:", "Ascension Exp:", and "Total Exp:" -- rather
  # than Field Exp. Field Exp is right for live pulse tracking (Daily
  # Grind) but wrong for long-term history: it's a bounded, self-draining
  # meter, not a record of lifetime progress. Experience/Ascension Exp are
  # the actual lifetime counters, and Total Exp is documented (and
  # confirmed against the user's own pasted numbers: 38,595,415 +
  # 16,981,703 = 55,577,118) to equal their exact sum, which this uses as
  # a cross-check -- see import_one_log_file. This only reads the .log
  # files that already exist on disk -- it never re-plays anything through
  # the game or the live DownstreamHook pipeline.
  #
  # Caveats, by design:
  #  - Day-level granularity only (each gain is bucketed under the
  #    calendar date in its filename, not the individual in-file
  #    timestamp) -- fine for week/month/year totals, not meant to
  #    reconstruct an hour-by-hour history.
  #  - The single most-recently-modified log file is always skipped, on
  #    the assumption it's today's still-open session -- that one is
  #    already covered by live tracking, and importing it too would
  #    double-count today's numbers.
  #  - Idempotent/incremental: each file's mtime+size is fingerprinted in
  #    history["processed_log_files"] once imported, so re-running this
  #    later only picks up files that are new or have grown since.
  def self.log_dir_for_character
    File.join(LOG_DIR, "#{XMLData.game}-#{Char.name}")
  end

  def self.import_history_from_logs!
    dir = log_dir_for_character
    return { total: 0, imported: 0, gained: 0 } unless Dir.exist?(dir)

    files = Dir.glob(File.join(dir, "**", "*.log")).sort_by { |f| File.mtime(f) }
    files.pop # skip the most recently modified file -- presumed still-open today's session

    processed = history["processed_log_files"]
    imported = 0
    total_gained = 0

    files.each do |path|
      fingerprint = "#{File.mtime(path).to_i}:#{File.size(path)}"
      next if processed[path] == fingerprint

      file_date = File.basename(path)[/\A(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})/, 1]
      next unless file_date

      total_gained += import_one_log_file(path, file_date)
      processed[path] = fingerprint
      imported += 1
    end

    self.history_dirty = true if imported > 0
    { total: files.size, imported: imported, gained: total_gained }
  end

  # Experience/Ascension Exp/Total Exp always print together as one
  # 3-line block in a real "experience" report, so gains are accumulated
  # as "pending" since the last Total Exp line, then only committed to
  # history once that same block's Total Exp line confirms
  # pending_exp + pending_asc == its own observed gain -- a mismatch means
  # a snapshot was missed (e.g. split across a session/log boundary) and
  # that batch is discarded rather than risk recording a wrong number.
  def self.import_one_log_file(path, file_date)
    content = File.read(path, encoding: "UTF-8", invalid: :replace, undef: :replace)
    prev_exp = nil
    prev_asc = nil
    prev_total = nil
    pending_exp = 0
    pending_asc = 0
    gained = 0

    content.each_line do |line|
      if line =~ /Experience:\s*([\d,]+)/
        val = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(",").to_i
        pending_exp += (val - prev_exp) if prev_exp && val > prev_exp
        prev_exp = val
      end

      if line =~ /Ascension Exp:\s*([\d,]+)/
        val = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(",").to_i
        pending_asc += (val - prev_asc) if prev_asc && val > prev_asc
        prev_asc = val
      end

      next unless line =~ /Total Exp:\s*([\d,]+)/

      val = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(",").to_i
      if prev_total && val > prev_total && (val - prev_total) == (pending_exp + pending_asc)
        if pending_exp > 0 || pending_asc > 0
          record_history_gain_for_date!(file_date, exp: pending_exp, asc: pending_asc)
          gained += pending_exp + pending_asc
        end
      end
      prev_total = val
      pending_exp = 0
      pending_asc = 0
    end

    gained
  rescue StandardError
    0
  end

  # date_string is "YYYY-MM-DD" from a log filename, with no time-of-day
  # to anchor to -- pinned to noon so it's nowhere near the 5 AM boundary
  # day_key/week_key/month_key/year_key adjust around, regardless of what
  # the DAY_BOUNDARY_HOUR constant happens to be.
  def self.record_history_gain_for_date!(date_string, exp: 0, asc: 0)
    year, month, day = date_string.split("-").map(&:to_i)
    at = Time.new(year, month, day, 12, 0, 0)
    record_history_gain!(exp: exp, asc: asc, at: at)
  rescue ArgumentError
    nil
  end

  def self.add_ignored!(key)
    key = key.to_s
    return false if ignored.include?(key)

    settings = load_settings
    self.ignored |= [key]
    settings["exp"]["ignored"] = ignored
    save_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.remove_ignored!(key)
    key = key.to_s
    return false unless ignored.include?(key)

    settings = load_settings
    self.ignored -= [key]
    settings["exp"]["ignored"] = ignored
    save_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.unignore_all!
    settings = load_settings
    self.ignored = []
    settings["exp"]["ignored"] = []
    save_settings(settings)
  end

  def self.sanitize_xml(text)
    text.to_s.gsub('&', '&amp;').gsub('<', '&lt;').gsub('>', '&gt;').gsub("'", '&apos;').gsub('"', '&quot;')
  end

  # Single dominant unit, same convention as treasurewindow.lic's
  # TreasureWindow.format_reset_time -- days while > 24h left, hours while
  # > 60m left, minutes once <= 60m left.
  def self.format_countdown(seconds_left)
    return "Ready" if seconds_left.nil? || seconds_left <= 0

    if seconds_left > 86400
      "#{seconds_left / 86400}d"
    elsif seconds_left > 3600
      hours = seconds_left / 3600
      hours < 24 ? "#{hours}h" : "#{seconds_left / 86400}d"
    else
      "#{[seconds_left / 60, 1].max}m"
    end
  end

  # Elapsed-since duration, e.g. "1h 42m" / "8m" -- used for "Active
  # (Xh Ym)" on Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage, which (unlike RPA) has both a
  # clean on and off trigger message, so this is a real elapsed duration
  # rather than a since-first-seen guess.
  def self.format_duration(seconds)
    total_minutes = (seconds / 60).to_i
    hours, minutes = total_minutes.divmod(60)
    hours > 0 ? "#{hours}h #{minutes}m" : "#{minutes}m"
  end

  def self.commas(n)
    n.nil? ? "--" : n.with_commas
  end

  # 5 AM-boundary-adjusted timestamp -- everything that buckets by
  # calendar period (today/this week/this month/this year) derives its key
  # from this same adjusted time, so a 2 AM gain consistently counts
  # toward the previous calendar day/week/month/year across all of them,
  # not just "today".
  def self.adjusted_time(time)
    time.hour < DAY_BOUNDARY_HOUR ? time - 86400 : time
  end

  def self.day_key(time)
    adjusted_time(time).strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
  end

  # ISO year-week (%G/%V), not %Y/%U -- avoids the late-December/
  # early-January edge case where a plain %Y-%U week number can roll over
  # a week early or late relative to the actual ISO week boundary.
  def self.week_key(time)
    adjusted_time(time).strftime("%G-W%V")
  end

  def self.month_key(time)
    adjusted_time(time).strftime("%Y-%m")
  end

  def self.year_key(time)
    adjusted_time(time).strftime("%Y")
  end

  def self.reset_today_if_new_day!(now)
    key = day_key(now)
    return if @data[:today_key] == key

    @data[:today_key] = key
    @data[:today_exp_gained] = 0
    @data[:today_asc_gained] = 0
    @data[:today_start_at] = now
  end

  def self.trim_history!
    cutoff = Time.now - HISTORY_KEEP_SECONDS
    @exp_history.reject! { |t, _| t < cutoff }
    @asc_history.reject! { |t, _| t < cutoff }
  end

  def self.last_hour_sum(samples)
    cutoff = Time.now - LAST_HOUR_SECONDS
    samples.select { |t, _| t >= cutoff }.sum { |_, gain| gain }
  end

  # elapsed hours since the 5 AM boundary, floored at 1 minute so a
  # just-opened panel doesn't divide by a near-zero interval and show a
  # wildly inflated rate.
  def self.elapsed_hours_today
    return 1.0 / 60 unless @data[:today_start_at]

    [(Time.now - @data[:today_start_at]) / 3600.0, 1.0 / 60].max
  end

  def self.avg_exp_per_hour
    return 0 unless @data[:today_exp_gained]

    (@data[:today_exp_gained] / elapsed_hours_today).to_i
  end

  def self.avg_asc_per_hour
    return 0 unless @data[:today_asc_gained]

    (@data[:today_asc_gained] / elapsed_hours_today).to_i
  end

  def self.eta_string(remaining, rate_per_hour)
    return "--" if remaining.nil? || rate_per_hour.nil? || rate_per_hour <= 0

    total_minutes = ((remaining.to_f / rate_per_hour) * 60).round
    hours, minutes = total_minutes.divmod(60)
    hours > 0 ? "~#{hours}h #{minutes}m" : "~#{minutes}m"
  end

  # Diff-based pulse/today/session tracking off the shared prev_field_exp/
  # prev_asc state -- called both from the passive expr-dialog observer
  # (fine-grained, real per-pulse deltas) and from the active *exp refresh
  # poll (coarse, but harmless since it diffs off whatever prev_field_exp
  # already is rather than accumulating independently -- if the passive
  # hook kept up, the active poll's delta is just ~0). track_pulse is
  # false for the active-poll call site so a 20-minute gap between polls
  # never gets misattributed as a single pulse for Exp/Pulse or Best Pulse.
  #
  # Driven off Field Exp, NOT the lifetime "Experience"/exp attribute --
  # same reason uberbar_eo.lic's own pulse tracking is driven off the
  # rotating TP-cycle counter in XMLData.next_level_text rather than a
  # lifetime total, and explicitly branches on `capped` (Stats.level ==
  # 100) to do it. At level 100 the lifetime Experience counter only jumps
  # in lump sums whenever a TP actually converts, and can sit frozen for a
  # long stretch in between -- Field Exp is what actually ticks nearly
  # every pulse regardless of level, so it's the correct always-live
  # signal. Field Exp also drains back down on its own over time as it
  # gets absorbed into your permanent pool (not just wrapping at its max),
  # so a DECREASE is normal and expected, not a "wrapped, reconstruct the
  # gain" case -- same as the exact skip-on-decrease behavior below.
  def self.record_exp_sample(new_field_exp, new_asc, track_pulse:)
    now = Time.now
    reset_today_if_new_day!(now)

    old_field_exp = @data[:prev_field_exp]
    old_asc = @data[:prev_asc]

    field_gain = (new_field_exp && old_field_exp && new_field_exp > old_field_exp) ? (new_field_exp - old_field_exp) : 0
    # Same bounded-meter sanity clamp as import_one_log_file -- Field Exp
    # can't legitimately jump by more than its own current max in one
    # tick, unlike Ascension Exp (no clamp below), which just grows.
    field_max = @data[:field_exp_max]
    field_gain = 0 if field_max && field_gain > field_max
    asc_gain = (new_asc && old_asc && new_asc > old_asc) ? (new_asc - old_asc) : 0

    if field_gain > 0
      @data[:today_exp_gained] = (@data[:today_exp_gained] || 0) + field_gain
      @exp_history << [now, field_gain]
    end

    if asc_gain > 0
      @data[:today_asc_gained] = (@data[:today_asc_gained] || 0) + asc_gain
      @asc_history << [now, asc_gain]
    end

    total_gain = field_gain + asc_gain
    if total_gain > 0
      record_history_gain!(field: field_gain, asc: asc_gain, at: now)
      if track_pulse
        @data[:last_pulse_gain] = total_gain
        @data[:best_pulse_gain] = [total_gain, @data[:best_pulse_gain] || 0].max
      end
    end

    @data[:prev_field_exp] = new_field_exp if new_field_exp
    @data[:prev_asc] = new_asc if new_asc

    trim_history!
  end

  # Separate from record_exp_sample -- feeds ONLY the persisted "exp"
  # history bucket (Experience This Week/Month/Year), never Daily Grind's
  # in-memory today/last-hour/pulse counters, which stay deliberately
  # Field-Exp-based. Called from both the passive expr-dialog observer and
  # the active *exp refresh poll, same as record_exp_sample, but there's
  # no track_pulse distinction here since nothing here is pulse-grained.
  def self.record_lifetime_exp_sample!(new_experience)
    old = @data[:prev_lifetime_exp]
    if new_experience && old && new_experience > old
      record_history_gain!(exp: new_experience - old, at: Time.now)
    end
    @data[:prev_lifetime_exp] = new_experience if new_experience
  end

  def self.row_value(key)
    d = @data
    case key
    when :level            then d[:level] ? d[:level].to_s : "--"
    when :experience       then commas(d[:experience])
    when :field_exp        then d[:field_exp] ? "#{commas(d[:field_exp])}/#{commas(d[:field_exp_max])}" : "--"
    when :ascension_exp    then commas(d[:ascension_exp])
    when :total_exp        then commas(d[:total_exp])
    when :long_term_exp    then commas(d[:long_term_exp])
    when :exp_next_tp      then commas(d[:exp_next_tp])
    when :eta_next_tp      then eta_string(d[:exp_next_tp], avg_exp_per_hour)
    when :exp_next_atp     then commas(d[:exp_next_atp])
    when :eta_next_atp     then eta_string(d[:exp_next_atp], avg_asc_per_hour)
    when :ptps_mtps        then (d[:ptps] || d[:mtps]) ? "#{d[:ptps] || '--'}/#{d[:mtps] || '--'}" : "--"
    when :atps             then d[:atps] ? d[:atps].to_s : "--"
    when :exp_today
      total = (d[:today_exp_gained] || 0) + (d[:today_asc_gained] || 0)
      (d[:today_exp_gained] || d[:today_asc_gained]) ? commas(total) : "--"
    when :avg_exp_hour
      (d[:today_exp_gained] || d[:today_asc_gained]) ? commas(avg_exp_per_hour + avg_asc_per_hour) : "--"
    when :exp_last_hour    then commas(last_hour_sum(@exp_history) + last_hour_sum(@asc_history))
    when :exp_per_pulse    then d[:last_pulse_gain] ? commas(d[:last_pulse_gain]) : "--"
    when :best_pulse       then d[:best_pulse_gain] ? commas(d[:best_pulse_gain]) : "--"
    when :hist_exp_week, :hist_exp_month, :hist_exp_year
      v = history_period_value(hist_period(key), "exp")
      v ? commas(v) : "--"
    when :hist_asc_week, :hist_asc_month, :hist_asc_year
      v = history_period_value(hist_period(key), "asc")
      v ? commas(v) : "--"
    when :hist_atp_week, :hist_atp_month, :hist_atp_year
      v = history_period_value(hist_period(key), "asc")
      v ? (v / ASCENSION_EXP_PER_ATP).to_s : "--"
    when :lumnis_donations then d[:lumnis_donations] || "Unknown (run *exp refresh)"
    when :lumnis_stage     then d[:lumnis_stage] || "Unknown (run *exp refresh)"
    when :lumnis_reset
      if d[:lumnis_reset_at].nil?
        "Unknown (run *exp refresh)"
      else
        format_countdown((d[:lumnis_reset_at] - Time.now).to_i)
      end
    when :fashlonae
      if d[:lumnis_cycle_active].nil? && d[:fashlonae].nil?
        "Unknown (run *exp refresh)"
      elsif d[:lumnis_cycle_active]
        # Per the user: while Lumnis's own weekly multiplier cycle is
        # still running (Lumnis Stage shows a tier in progress), Tutelage
        # isn't actually granting anything yet regardless of what the
        # fashlonae flag says -- it only starts once that cycle ends, so
        # this is "lined up for it," not "receiving it."
        "Eligible"
      elsif d[:fashlonae] == true
        # Lumnis is done for the week -- fashlonae now reflects whether
        # Tutelage is genuinely active for real.
        d[:fashlonae_since] ? "Active (#{format_duration(Time.now - d[:fashlonae_since])})" : "Active"
      else
        "Ineligible"
      end
    when :rpa then d[:rpa] ? "Active (*exp clearrpa to reset)" : "--"
    when :resource_type
      type = d[:resource_type]
      (type.nil? || type.to_s.strip.empty?) ? "None detected" : type.to_s
    when :resource_weekly
      d[:resource_weekly] ? "#{commas(d[:resource_weekly])}/50k" : "--"
    when :resource_total
      d[:resource_total] ? "#{commas(d[:resource_total])}/200k" : "--"
    end
  end

  # Only :lumnis_stage's label varies -- "Lumnis Stage x2:" while a tier
  # is in progress (per the user's own x2/x3/x4/x5 numbering, matching
  # TIER_STAGE), otherwise the plain "Lumnis Stage:" ROW_LABELS default.
  def self.row_label(key)
    if key == :lumnis_stage && @data[:lumnis_stage_num]
      "Lumnis Stage x#{@data[:lumnis_stage_num]}"
    else
      ROW_LABELS[key]
    end
  end

  def self.build_dialog
    out = String.new("<dialogData id='ExpPanel' clear='t'>")
    top = 0
    pending_spacer_key = nil

    SECTIONS.each_with_index do |(title, keys), section_idx|
      visible_keys = keys.reject { |key| ignored.include?(key.to_s) || (RESOURCE_KEYS.include?(key) && !resource_enabled) }
      next if visible_keys.empty?

      if pending_spacer_key && !ignored.include?(pending_spacer_key)
        out << "<label id='exp_spc_#{pending_spacer_key}' value='' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' width='#{LABEL_WIDTH + value_width}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        unless hide_arrows
          out << "<link id='exp_spc_x_#{pending_spacer_key}' value='#{REMOVE_ICON}' cmd='*exp ignore #{pending_spacer_key}' justify='left' left='#{remove_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{REMOVE_WIDTH}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        end
        top += ROW_HEIGHT
      end
      pending_spacer_key = nil

      out << "<link id='exp_hdr_#{section_idx}' value='#{sanitize_xml("-- #{title} --")}' cmd='' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' width='#{LABEL_WIDTH + value_width + REMOVE_WIDTH}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      top += ROW_HEIGHT

      visible_keys.each do |key|
        label = row_label(key)
        out << "<label id='exp_lbl_#{key}' value='#{sanitize_xml("#{label}:")}' justify='left' left='#{LABEL_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{LABEL_WIDTH}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        if key == :field_exp
          # Field Exp specifically -- link instead of label (so the
          # panel's font-override/color Settings actually apply, same
          # reason commspanel_sagapanel.lic's rows are links). Tried
          # wrapping the value in a real <output class="mono"/>...
          # <output class=""/> pair (the same one the "experience"
          # command's own report uses) -- confirmed NOT to work: Saga's
          # dialog widget value attribute isn't parsed as XML the way the
          # main text stream is, so it just showed the literal tag text
          # instead of applying mono formatting. Reverted to plain text
          # value; font='mono' as a widget attribute is unconfirmed too
          # (no precedent anywhere else in this codebase), so it's left
          # off rather than guessed at again. cmd is a real action (*exp
          # refresh), not a throwaway required-attribute filler.
          out << "<link id='exp_val_#{key}' value='#{sanitize_xml(row_value(key))}' cmd='*exp refresh' justify='left' left='#{VALUE_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{value_width}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        else
          out << "<label id='exp_val_#{key}' value='#{sanitize_xml(row_value(key))}' justify='left' left='#{VALUE_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{value_width}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        end
        unless hide_arrows
          out << "<link id='exp_x_#{key}' value='#{REMOVE_ICON}' cmd='*exp ignore #{key}' justify='left' left='#{remove_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{REMOVE_WIDTH}' height='#{ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        end
        top += ROW_HEIGHT
      end

      pending_spacer_key = SPACER_KEYS[section_idx]
    end
    out << "</dialogData>"
    out
  end

  def self.snapshot
    ROW_KEYS.map { |key| row_value(key) } + [ignored.sort, resource_enabled, hide_arrows]
  end

  # Passive parse of the game's own native experience-bar dialog -- no
  # command sent, updates whenever the client itself refreshes that
  # widget (e.g. every pulse while it's open).
  def self.observe_expr_dialog(server_string)
    return unless server_string.include?("dialogData id='expr'") || server_string.include?('dialogData id="expr"')

    if server_string =~ /value=['"]Level (\d+)['"]/
      @data[:level] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    if server_string =~ /field_exp=['"](\d+)['"]/
      @data[:field_exp] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    if server_string =~ /max_field_exp=['"](\d+)['"]/
      @data[:field_exp_max] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    if server_string =~ /ascension_exp=['"](\d+)['"]/
      @data[:ascension_exp] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    if server_string =~ /fashlonae=['"](\d+)['"]/
      new_fashlonae = (Regexp.last_match(1) == "1")
      # fashlonae_since is only ever stamped by the exact on/off trigger
      # text (see observe_tutelage_text) -- this attribute alone can arrive
      # already showing fashlonae='1' on script start (Tutelage was active
      # before the panel opened), where we genuinely don't know when it
      # started, so we only ever clear the timestamp here, never set it.
      @data[:fashlonae_since] = nil unless new_fashlonae
      @data[:fashlonae] = new_fashlonae
    end
    if server_string =~ /\bexp=['"](\d+)['"]/
      @data[:experience] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    if server_string =~ /until_next=['"](\d+)['"]/
      @data[:exp_next_tp] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    end
    record_exp_sample(@data[:field_exp], @data[:ascension_exp], track_pulse: true)
    record_lifetime_exp_sample!(@data[:experience])
    @data[:last_updated] = Time.now
  end

  # Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage has exact, symmetric on/off narrative lines
  # (confirmed against gswiki.play.net/Fash'lo'nae's_Tutelage), unlike RPA
  # which only ever announces itself turning on. Checked against every
  # downstream line, not just expr-dialog ones, since these are plain
  # narrative text, not part of that dialog.
  TUTELAGE_ON_RX = /You feel a heightened understanding of events around you\./.freeze
  TUTELAGE_OFF_RX = /The feeling of heightened understanding departs, leaving behind a cold hunger for forbidden knowledge that is slow to fade\./.freeze

  def self.observe_tutelage_text(server_string)
    if server_string =~ TUTELAGE_ON_RX
      @data[:fashlonae] = true
      @data[:fashlonae_since] = Time.now
    elsif server_string =~ TUTELAGE_OFF_RX
      @data[:fashlonae] = false
      @data[:fashlonae_since] = nil
    end
  end

  # Blocks (with a hard timeout, unlike wait_until) until block returns
  # true, then makes sure hook_id is torn down either way. Used instead of
  # wait_until because a scoop hook can otherwise sit registered forever
  # if its anchor line never shows (e.g. the put command got eaten by
  # roundtime/a lock).
  def self.wait_for_capture(hook_id, timeout: 15)
    deadline = Time.now + timeout
    until yield || Time.now >= deadline
      sleep 0.25
    end
  ensure
    DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
  end

  # Both scoops below extract fields directly off each recognized line as
  # it arrives, the same way lumnismon.lic's own scoop procs do, rather
  # than buffering everything from put until the next <prompt> and
  # regex-scanning the blob afterward. That blob approach used to swallow
  # (and lose) any unrelated concurrent traffic -- room events, other
  # players' actions, anything with its own <prompt> -- landing between
  # our put and the real response, and a busy moment could make that
  # unrelated prompt arrive FIRST, ending the capture before our
  # command's actual response ever printed (silent failure, only ever
  # working while nothing else was happening). Matching on each field's
  # own distinct wording instead means capture only starts once we've
  # actually seen real command output, and anything unrecognized always
  # passes through untouched rather than getting swallowed on a guess.
  def self.refresh_experience!
    done = false
    filter = false
    hook_id = "exppanel_capture_experience"
    DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
    DownstreamHook.add(hook_id, proc do |server_string|
      case server_string
      when /^\s*Level:\s*(\d+)\s+Fame:/
        filter = true
        @data[:level] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
        next(nil)
      when /^\s*$/
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Experience:\s*([\d,]+)\s+Field Exp:\s*([\d,]+)\/([\d,]+)/
        if filter
          @data[:experience] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i
          @data[:field_exp] = Regexp.last_match(2).delete(',').to_i
          @data[:field_exp_max] = Regexp.last_match(3).delete(',').to_i
        end
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Ascension Exp:\s*([\d,]+)/
        @data[:ascension_exp] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Total Exp:\s*([\d,]+)/
        @data[:total_exp] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Long-Term Exp:\s*([\d,]+)/
        @data[:long_term_exp] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Exp to next TP:\s*([\d,]+)\s+Exp to next ATP:\s*([\d,]+)/
        if filter
          @data[:exp_next_tp] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i
          @data[:exp_next_atp] = Regexp.last_match(2).delete(',').to_i
        end
        next(nil) if filter
      when %r{PTPs/MTPs:\s*(\d+)/(\d+)\s+ATPs:\s*(\d+)}
        if filter
          @data[:ptps] = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
          @data[:mtps] = Regexp.last_match(2).to_i
          @data[:atps] = Regexp.last_match(3).to_i
        end
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Your recent adventures echo powerfully in your mind\./
        @data[:rpa] = true if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /^<prompt time=/
        if filter
          DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id)
          done = true
        end
        next(server_string)
      else
        next(server_string)
      end
      server_string
    end)
    silence_me
    put "experience"
    silence_me
    wait_for_capture(hook_id) { done }
    record_exp_sample(@data[:field_exp], @data[:ascension_exp], track_pulse: false)
    record_lifetime_exp_sample!(@data[:experience])
    @data[:last_updated] = Time.now
  end

  def self.refresh_lumnis!
    done = false
    filter = false
    lumnis_result = nil
    hook_id = "exppanel_capture_lumnis"
    DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
    DownstreamHook.add(hook_id, proc do |server_string|
      case server_string
      # The tier-in-progress/ready/f2p sentence and the "scheduled to
      # refresh in..." sentence are one combined server line (same as
      # lumnismon.lic observes) -- stash the whole thing and split it on
      # "." afterward rather than trying to match both halves as separate
      # case branches, since only the first match wins in a case/when.
      when /It is scheduled to refresh|restart as soon as you absorb experience|Because your account is free,/
        filter = true
        lumnis_result = server_string
        next(nil)
      when /^\s*$/
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Your Gift of Lumnis has expired for this week\./
        if filter
          @data[:lumnis_stage] = "Expired this week"
          @data[:lumnis_stage_num] = nil
          @data[:lumnis_cycle_active] = false
        end
        next(nil) if filter
      when /You have made ([\d,]+) recent donations to the Temple of Lumnis\./
        @data[:lumnis_donations] = Regexp.last_match(1) if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /You have not made any recent donations to the Temple of Lumnis\./
        @data[:lumnis_donations] = "None" if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /not presently receiving Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage/
        @data[:fashlonae] = false if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /Fash'lo'nae's Tutelage/
        @data[:fashlonae] = true if filter
        next(nil) if filter
      when /^<prompt time=/
        if filter
          DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id)
          done = true
        end
        next(server_string)
      else
        next(server_string)
      end
      server_string
    end)
    silence_me
    put "lumnis info"
    silence_me
    wait_for_capture(hook_id) { done }
    parse_lumnis_result!(lumnis_result) if lumnis_result
    @data[:last_updated] = Time.now
  end

  # lumnis_result is the single combined sentence captured above, e.g.
  # "You have 5,713 points of doubled experience remaining. It is
  # scheduled to refresh in 5 days, 3 hours, 12 minutes." -- split on "."
  # the same way lumnismon.lic's parse_result_array does.
  def self.parse_lumnis_result!(lumnis_result)
    if lumnis_result =~ /restart as soon as you absorb experience/
      @data[:lumnis_stage] = "Ready (restarts on next exp)"
      @data[:lumnis_stage_num] = nil
      @data[:lumnis_cycle_active] = false
      @data[:lumnis_reset_at] = Time.now
      return
    end

    sentences = lumnis_result.split(".")

    if sentences[0] =~ /([\d,]+)\s+points? of (tripled|doubled|quadrupled|quintupled) experience/
      pts = Regexp.last_match(1)
      tier = Regexp.last_match(2)
      # Stage number goes in the row's LABEL ("Lumnis Stage x2:"), not the
      # value, so the value can just be the pts count instead of repeating
      # "Stage 2 (doubled)" and stretching the panel wider than it needs.
      @data[:lumnis_stage_num] = TIER_STAGE[tier]
      @data[:lumnis_stage] = "#{pts} pts"
      @data[:lumnis_cycle_active] = true
    end

    time_part = sentences[1].to_s
    days = time_part[/(\d+)\s*days?/, 1].to_i
    hours = time_part[/(\d+)\s*hours?/, 1].to_i
    minutes = time_part[/(\d+)\s*minutes?/, 1].to_i
    total_seconds = (days * 86400) + (hours * 3600) + (minutes * 60)
    @data[:lumnis_reset_at] = Time.now + total_seconds if total_seconds > 0
  end

  def self.refresh_all!
    refresh_experience!
    refresh_lumnis!
  end

  # Lich::Resources.check (lib/attributes/resources.rb) is
  # professionresource_sagapanel.lic's own data source -- same
  # Lich::Util.issue_command-based "resource" scoop that script already
  # relies on, so this reuses it directly instead of hand-rolling another
  # capture. Like refresh_experience!/refresh_lumnis!, issue_command reads
  # Script.current internally, so this can only ever be called from the
  # script's own thread (main loop), never from inside the UpstreamHook
  # proc -- same reasoning as manual_refresh_requested below.
  def self.refresh_resource!
    Lich::Resources.check(true)
    @data[:resource_type] = Lich::Resources.type
    @data[:resource_weekly] = Lich::Resources.weekly
    @data[:resource_total] = Lich::Resources.total
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # refresh_experience!/refresh_lumnis!'s put/silence_me/wait_for_capture
  # all resolve Script.current off the calling thread's identity, which
  # only ever resolves correctly
  # from the script's own thread (its top-level body, or the loop at the
  # bottom of this file) -- NOT from inside an UpstreamHook proc, which
  # runs on whatever thread is feeding it upstream commands and has no
  # script identity of its own ("silence_me: cannot identify calling
  # script."). So *exp refresh can't call refresh_all! directly from the
  # hook; it just flips this flag, and the script's own main loop (below)
  # does the actual refresh on its next tick.
  @manual_refresh_requested = false
  # Same reasoning as manual_refresh_requested -- *exp importlogs reads
  # File I/O only (no Script.current dependency), but scanning hundreds of
  # log files can take a noticeable moment, and running that inline inside
  # the UpstreamHook proc would stall processing of any other upstream
  # commands until it finishes. Queued and run from the main loop instead.
  @log_import_requested = false
  # Same reasoning again -- set when *exp resource just turned the feature
  # on, so the main loop polls Lich::Resources.check immediately instead
  # of leaving the new rows showing "--" for up to RESOURCE_POLL_SECONDS.
  @resource_poll_requested = false

  class << self
    attr_accessor :manual_refresh_requested, :log_import_requested, :resource_poll_requested
  end

  def self.request_manual_refresh!
    self.manual_refresh_requested = true
  end

  def self.request_log_import!
    self.log_import_requested = true
  end

  def self.request_resource_poll!
    self.resource_poll_requested = true
  end
end

@exp_settings = ExpPanel.load_settings
ExpPanel.ignored = @exp_settings["exp"]["ignored"]
ExpPanel.value_width = @exp_settings["exp"]["value_width"]
ExpPanel.resource_enabled = @exp_settings["exp"]["resource_enabled"]
ExpPanel.hide_arrows = @exp_settings["exp"]["hide_arrows"]

ExpPanel.load_history!
# reset_today_if_new_day! must run first to stamp today_key -- otherwise
# the next real gain event would see today_key unset, treat it as a new
# day, and immediately zero back out what restore_today_from_history!
# just restored.
ExpPanel.reset_today_if_new_day!(Time.now)
ExpPanel.restore_today_from_history!

exp_downstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_downstream"
DownstreamHook.remove(exp_downstream_hook_id) rescue nil
DownstreamHook.add(exp_downstream_hook_id, proc do |server_string|
  ExpPanel.observe_expr_dialog(server_string)
  ExpPanel.observe_tutelage_text(server_string)
  server_string
end)

exp_upstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_upstream"
UpstreamHook.remove(exp_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
UpstreamHook.add(exp_upstream_hook_id, proc do |command|
  case command.strip
  when /\*exp\s+refresh\s*\z/i
    ExpPanel.request_manual_refresh!
    respond "Exp Panel: refreshing..."
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+importlogs\s*\z/i
    ExpPanel.request_log_import!
    respond "Exp Panel: scanning your session logs for historical Exp This Week/Month/Year data..."
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+ignore\s+(\S+)\s*\z/i
    key = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
    unless (ExpPanel::ROW_KEYS.map(&:to_s) + ExpPanel::SPACER_KEYS).include?(key)
      respond "Exp Panel: unknown field '#{key}'"
      next(nil)
    end
    if ExpPanel.add_ignored!(key)
      _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
      respond "Exp Panel: hiding '#{key}'"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel: already hiding '#{key}'"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+unignore\s+all\s*\z/i
    ExpPanel.unignore_all!
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    respond "Exp Panel: no longer hiding anything"
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+unignore\s+(\S+)\s*\z/i
    key = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
    if ExpPanel.remove_ignored!(key)
      _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
      respond "Exp Panel: no longer hiding '#{key}'"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel: wasn't hiding '#{key}'"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+ignored\s*\z/i
    if ExpPanel.ignored.empty?
      respond "Exp Panel: nothing hidden"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel hidden fields: #{ExpPanel.ignored.sort.join(', ')}"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+tracked\s*\z/i
    shown = ExpPanel::ROW_KEYS.map(&:to_s) - ExpPanel.ignored
    if shown.empty?
      respond "Exp Panel: nothing shown (everything hidden)"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel shown fields: #{shown.join(', ')}"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+clearrpa\s*\z/i
    ExpPanel.data[:rpa] = false
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    respond "Exp Panel: RPA indicator cleared"
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+width\s+(\d+)\s*\z/i
    width = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    if ExpPanel.set_value_width!(width)
      _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
      respond "Exp Panel: value column width set to #{width} (mirrors *tm width in timers_sagapanel.lic -- enter the same number there for a matching look)"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel: width must be a positive number"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+resource\s*\z/i
    enabled = ExpPanel.set_resource_enabled!(!ExpPanel.resource_enabled)
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    if enabled
      ExpPanel.request_resource_poll!
      respond "Exp Panel: profession resource display on -- polling..."
    else
      respond "Exp Panel: profession resource display off"
    end
    nil
  when /\*exp\s+hidearrows\s*\z/i
    hidden = ExpPanel.toggle_hide_arrows!
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    respond "Exp Panel: hide arrows #{hidden ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil
  else
    command
  end
end)

_respond("<closeDialog id='ExpPanel'/><openDialog type='dynamic' id='ExpPanel' title='Experience' target='ExpPanel' scroll='manual' location='main' resident='true'><dialogData id='ExpPanel'></dialogData></openDialog>")
ExpPanel.refresh_all!
_respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)

before_dying do
  ExpPanel.save_history!
  UpstreamHook.remove(exp_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
  DownstreamHook.remove(exp_downstream_hook_id) rescue nil
  _respond("<closeDialog id='ExpPanel'/>")
end

echo "Exp Panel is active."

@exp_last_snapshot = ExpPanel.snapshot
@exp_last_refresh_at = Time.now
@exp_last_active_poll_at = Time.now
@exp_last_history_save_at = Time.now
@exp_last_resource_poll_at = Time.at(0)

loop do
  if ExpPanel.manual_refresh_requested
    ExpPanel.manual_refresh_requested = false
    ExpPanel.refresh_all!
    @exp_last_active_poll_at = Time.now
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    respond "Exp Panel: refreshed"
  elsif (Time.now - @exp_last_active_poll_at) > (20 * 60)
    ExpPanel.refresh_all!
    @exp_last_active_poll_at = Time.now
  end

  if ExpPanel.resource_enabled &&
     (ExpPanel.resource_poll_requested || (Time.now - @exp_last_resource_poll_at) > ExpPanel::RESOURCE_POLL_SECONDS)
    ExpPanel.resource_poll_requested = false
    ExpPanel.refresh_resource!
    @exp_last_resource_poll_at = Time.now
  end

  if ExpPanel.log_import_requested
    ExpPanel.log_import_requested = false
    result = ExpPanel.import_history_from_logs!
    ExpPanel.save_history!
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
    if result[:imported].zero?
      respond "Exp Panel: no new/changed log files to import (#{result[:total]} already up to date)"
    else
      respond "Exp Panel: imported #{result[:imported]} of #{result[:total]} log file(s), " \
              "added #{result[:gained].with_commas} exp to history"
    end
  end

  # Throttled -- record_exp_sample can flag history dirty on nearly every
  # pulse, and save_history! itself no-ops when nothing changed, so this
  # just caps how often that write actually hits disk.
  if (Time.now - @exp_last_history_save_at) > 60
    ExpPanel.save_history!
    @exp_last_history_save_at = Time.now
  end

  snapshot = ExpPanel.snapshot
  if snapshot != @exp_last_snapshot || (Time.now - @exp_last_refresh_at) > 30.0
    @exp_last_snapshot = snapshot
    @exp_last_refresh_at = Time.now
    _respond(ExpPanel.build_dialog)
  end
  sleep 1
end
